#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422481} :activity/id #uuid "fda0e0b8-3081-5e52-8593-c6700e3052bb" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048742 :topic/id #uuid "ba72c50b-60dc-50dc-ae9b-3cc018d38d60" :topic/math-academy-id 1049} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422480 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee5bd89-c4e9-5aea-ba6a-3f045af5c0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422467} {:answer/id #uuid "75130a5b-9607-5217-b80c-6757c94daf70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422471} {:answer/id #uuid "8076b85b-1614-5135-bb4c-2ab5d41377da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422472} {:answer/id #uuid "d64479b7-f216-5594-be33-53f9d09c2c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422473} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ebe9c7-57ca-5f13-b184-b18fa5a512d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422475}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422472} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4a2cf38-1593-52f1-9b63-551383c8a50f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "df6c8a6d-153a-5484-848d-1043ee95c582" :question/math-academy-id "q-74621" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-11y+5z=-1 \\\\ x-3y+2z=1 \\\\ -3x+9y-6z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -11 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -11 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -11 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "06ed1b32-abf8-5d02-b409-e83aa1a9bf69" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422482}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422481 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f53140c-1654-5c33-b318-d2cc5cdbf3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨3,2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416405} {:answer/id #uuid "3b8ed053-8c5f-5809-b29d-46bc30062dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨3,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416409} {:answer/id #uuid "52ed3b97-c09d-5bac-bedf-d8cb30fd9295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416411} {:answer/id #uuid "ad204329-d0a2-52cb-bab5-d155cba3473f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416423} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5e31d8-6742-527d-a027-3e41d829bbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,-2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416428}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416409} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9c6d72-c8a0-5fe2-aea3-51adff0f94d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cb5d2e37-01c6-52dc-86a3-0e3d22b79684" :question/math-academy-id "q-20267" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=2 \\\\  & x+2y+z=0 \\\\  & x+y+2z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=3 \\\\  & y=-2 \\\\  & z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=3$, $y=-2$, and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨3,-2,1⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "1f437206-fa08-5382-b319-4b882827b9a2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422483}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422482 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266102 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "083caf03-1501-5cba-8190-446a66b010a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-2,3,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263075} {:answer/id #uuid "9af8bfe2-063c-5dba-b504-5816b98f9766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264325} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b913e9-5eb2-5d55-9bc3-2f3b88be543b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264598} {:answer/id #uuid "da1a8356-2e88-513c-b7fa-151c2d4478c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨3,-2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264902} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e3c0bf-feab-56d8-8788-d7833ba1031b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-2,3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265152}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264325} :answer-field/id #uuid "71bd9945-c16d-52b1-9144-9035edc43bba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ff5175c-29cf-5e1c-8b8a-50a809738a87" :question/math-academy-id "q-131618" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=5 \\\\  & 2x-y+7z=7 \\\\  & x-y+3z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=2 \\\\  & y=-3 \\\\  & z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=2$, $y=-3$, and $z=0.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨2,-3,0⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "6862e7b5-f79b-5b64-a612-6d85862752ef" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422484}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422483 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47f1079e-5752-5de3-a9e1-e19c06fada97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339766} {:answer/id #uuid "599056ef-e9ef-5488-965a-9dd9e4140202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339942} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e2972b-b0c5-5496-8789-531b77f4e97c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340614} {:answer/id #uuid "bac13010-faae-5ec6-a632-601054299d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340802} {:answer/id #uuid "f4632778-f58f-50b4-b85c-9458c6830a8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341280}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340614} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5965582-0f9c-5d43-87a1-fef40d8e1c11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a1acb1c2-35d8-56f8-bcad-3b6d0c4f6e46" :question/math-academy-id "q-74601" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=3 \\\\  & -2x-3y+2z=0 \\\\  & 2x+3y-z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6e7d6a76-cc67-5b59-8e1b-d53698eacff0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422480}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422484 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7564c8-04d6-57a1-9a06-28d7b8421a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}y+2z+2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422466} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1f7437-d98a-5bd7-97a0-2e5ff4f2f649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422468} {:answer/id #uuid "41cef48b-98a3-54bd-b406-d5e167d64ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-y+2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422469} {:answer/id #uuid "45df3fe7-8c4e-5624-afa2-3e1ab32743c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}y-2z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422470} {:answer/id #uuid "d82b73e6-0a25-5302-99e8-b157a818667e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}y-2z-1 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422474}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422470} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d6b9331-1da4-5d89-9d4a-e8d26ffe05e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "86e15f08-648b-5bcc-988f-7551732eb466" :question/math-academy-id "q-131649" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y-4z=4 \\\\ -x+y-2z=2 \\\\ x-y+2z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=y-2z-2 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}y-2z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9f34ebb7-b2e8-595a-840d-d43ea1cd168d"}] :activity/title "Reduced Row Echelon Form" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422465}]}
